In 30 seconds, please choose all the correct answers to this question.

42
00:03:05,490 --> 00:03:07,690
Your time starts now.

43
00:03:10,410 --> 00:03:12,910
From the sample paragraph at the beginning of today's lesson, 

44
00:03:12,910 --> 00:03:18,750
we can see that a topic sentence carries the main idea of the whole

45
00:03:18,750 --> 00:03:24,890
paragraph and other sentences will support, explain or illustrate the topic sentence.

46
00:03:25,730 --> 00:03:29,870
Remember, all information in the paragraph must be

47
00:03:29,870 --> 00:03:36,190
related to the topic sentence, so we cannot have  one or two unrelated or off-topic

48
00:03:36,190 --> 00:03:37,730
sentences in the paragraph.

49
00:03:38,970 --> 00:03:42,290
And certainly, you must write this sentence very clearly, 

50
00:03:42,290 --> 00:03:48,710
but not imply something and then hope that the examiner will read and understand it on their own.

51
00:03:49,530 --> 00:03:52,530
Don't challenge the examiner to do matching headings.

52
00:03:54,770 --> 00:03:57,450
A topic sentence only presents the main idea

53
00:03:57,450 --> 00:04:00,010
of the paragraph without explaining it.

54
00:04:00,370 --> 00:04:00,630
Correct!

55
00:04:01,770 --> 00:04:05,050
The topic sentence only summarizes the main idea

56
00:04:05,050 --> 00:04:07,290
of the paragraph, so it should not be

57
00:04:07,290 --> 00:04:08,570
wordy or lengthy.

58
00:04:09,390 --> 00:04:12,490
Explaining is the function of the following sentences.

59
00:04:13,550 --> 00:04:17,209
Also, from the previous lesson, the most effective

60
00:04:17,209 --> 00:04:20,089
way of writing paragraphs in IELTS writing test

